# Node/TS testing

- Prefer `vitest` over `jest` for new TS projects — same API, ~10x faster, native ESM.
- No shared mutable state across test files. Each test file must be runnable in isolation and in parallel.
- Mock at the module boundary, not at the syscall. `vi.mock("./api")` beats `vi.spyOn(fetch)`.
- Use `describe` blocks sparingly. Tests should read as flat, self-describing sentences.
- Playwright: use `test.step()` to break long flows into named phases. Test failures point straight at the phase.
- No implicit waits (`page.waitForTimeout(500)`). Use locator auto-waiting or explicit `expect(locator).toBeVisible()`.
- Snapshot tests are a smell 90% of the time. Assert on the meaningful shape, not the whole DOM.
- Every `expect()` in an async test needs `await` if the matcher is async. `await expect(page).toHaveURL(...)`.
- Do not test third-party libraries. Test YOUR usage of them.
